<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Seival</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1836">1836</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ragamuffin-war">Ragamuffin War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Seival was fought on 10 September 1836 near Bagé in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rio-grande-do-sul">Rio Grande do Sul</a>, where rebel forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonio-de-sousa-neto">Antônio de Sousa Neto</a> defeated an imperial column. The following day Neto proclaimed the independent Riograndense Republic, turning the Ragamuffin revolt into a separatist war against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-seival.jpg" alt="Battle of Seival" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antônio Parreiras · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Antonio_Parreiras_-_Proclama%C3%A7%C3%A3o_da_Rep%C3%BAblica_Piratini_-_1915.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
